{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"role":"assistant","content":{"type":"text","text":"Key considerations for Mrs. Davis this morning:\n\n1. FALL RISK — overnight bed exit at 02:14 (47 seconds, self-resolved) combined with high MDS fall-risk classification requires mobility assessment before ambulation. Confirm bed rails and call light are within reach.\n\n2. SLEEP QUALITY — elevated movement index (7.2) during 04:52 window may indicate discomfort, pain, or anxiety. Perform brief mood and pain screen during greeting.\n\n3. BLOOD PRESSURE — last reading 118/72 at 20:00. Lisinopril is on-schedule; confirm BP before administering to rule out morning hypotension (target systolic ≥100 per facility protocol).\n\n4. COGNITIVE CHECK — MCI diagnosis: use orientation cues and simple one-step instructions. Avoid rushing during medication administration.\n\n5. DIABETES MONITORING — Metformin due; verify resident has eaten or will eat within 30 minutes to prevent GI adverse effects."},"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stopReason":"end_turn"}}
