{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":11,"result":{"role":"assistant","content":{"type":"text","text":"END-OF-ROUNDS SUMMARY — Mrs. Eleanor Davis (RES-00142, Room 214B)\n\nSTATUS: Stable with active monitoring flags.\n\nCOMPLETED THIS ROUND:\n• Metformin 500mg ✓ administered\n• Aspirin 81mg ✓ administered  \n• Clinical note documented (Note ID: NOTE-20250608-0819)\n• MDS Sections C, D, G, N updated\n\nOPEN ITEMS REQUIRING FOLLOW-UP:\n1. [HIGH] Lisinopril 10mg HELD — BP 102/64 at 08:14. Charge nurse notified (ALT-20250608-0814). Recheck BP by 10:00; administer or defer per physician protocol.\n2. [MEDIUM] New tremor observation (bilateral, hands) — not previously documented. Flag for physical therapy referral and physician awareness. May require medication review (metformin-associated B12 deficiency is a differential).\n3. [MEDIUM] Bed exit at 02:14 overnight — reinforced fall prevention measures in place. Recommend night staff increase bed-check frequency.\n4. [LOW] PHQ-9 score 2 — resident engaged and looking forward to afternoon music group. No mood intervention needed today.\n\nNEXT SCHEDULED CONTACT: 10:00 BP recheck by charge nurse or designee."},"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stopReason":"end_turn"}}
